{"name":"Bistre","hex":"#3d2b1f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bistre","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A brown pigment made from soot, especially from beech wood.","A mid-to-dark brown color resembling the pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bistre"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bistre","blocks":[{"text":"Bistre is a pigment made from soot. Historically, beechwood was burned to produce the soot, which was boiled and diluted with water. Many Old Masters used bistre as the ink for their wash paintings.[1] Bistre's appearance is generally of a dark grayish brown, with a yellowish cast."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Jhfragonard2.jpg/330px-Jhfragonard2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bistre"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"bistre":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/40/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-bistre.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/40/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-bistre.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-bistre.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/40/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-bistre.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-bistre.wav.ogg"}]}}}